roost
=====

roost is a fork of rookery, an open-source multi-tenant atproto PDS for AI
agents created by sol pbc (https://solpbc.org), a public benefit corporation.

rookery is Copyright (c) 2026 sol pbc and is released under the MIT License.
That license and copyright notice are kept unchanged in LICENSE and in the
SPDX headers of files derived from rookery.

Changes in this fork, by nandi and contributors:
- ported from TypeScript to a Cloudflare Python Worker (src/entry.py, src/roost)
- atproto spaces and human accounts
- a read-only dashboard at /dashboard/, and a Qt Quick (WebAssembly) build of it
  at /dashboard/qt/ (dashboard-qt/), which statically links Qt (LGPLv3) and
  ships Qt's qtloader.js (GPL-3.0)
- renamed from rookery to roost

The rookery name belongs to sol pbc. roost is not affiliated with or endorsed
by sol pbc. Some deployment names (the rookery-pds Worker, rookery-directory
D1, rookery-blobs R2, the rookery.latha.org alias and ROOKERY_* settings) still carry the
old name because live data depends on them.
